      "text": "To solve the problem of finding the base seven product of \\(24_7\\) and \\(30_7\\) and then determining the base seven sum of the digits of that product, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Convert the base seven numbers to base ten.\n2. Multiply the base ten equivalents.\n3. Convert the product back to base seven.\n4. Find the sum of the digits of the product in base seven.\n\n**Step 1: Convert \\(24_7\\) to base ten.**\n\nThe base seven number \\(24_7\\) can be expressed in base ten as:\n\\[24_7 = 2 \\cdot 7^1 + 4 \\cdot 7^0 = 2 \\cdot 7 + 4 \\cdot 1 = 14 + 4 = 18_{10}.\\]\n\n**Step 2: Convert \\(30_7\\) to base ten.**\n\nThe base seven number \\(30_7\\) can be expressed in base ten as:\n\\[30_7 = 3 \\cdot 7^1 + 0 \\cdot 7^0 = 3 \\cdot 7 + 0 \\cdot 1 = 21 + 0 = 21_{10}.\\]\n\n**Step 3: Multiply the base ten equivalents.**\n\nNow, we multiply the base ten equivalents:\n\\[18_{10} \\times 21_{10} = 378_{10}.\\]\n\n**Step 4: Convert \\(378_{10}\\) back to base seven.**\n\nTo convert \\(378_{10}\\) to base seven, we need to divide by 7 and keep track of the remainders:\n\\[378 \\div 7 = 54 \\text{ remainder } 0,\\]\n\\[54 \\div 7 = 7 \\text{ remainder } 5,\\]\n\\[7 \\div 7 = 1 \\text{ remainder } 0,\\]\n\\[1 \\div 7 = 0 \\text{ remainder } 1.\\]\nReading the remainders from bottom to top, we get \\(378_{10} = 1050_7\\).\n\n**Step 5: Find the sum of the digits of the product in base seven.**\n\nThe base seven number \\(1050_7\\) has digits 1, 0, 5, and 0. The sum of these digits is:\n\\[1 + 0 + 5 + 0 = 6.\\]\n\nTherefore, the base seven sum of the digits of the product is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).",
