      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Convert the base 7 numbers \\(24_7\\) and \\(30_7\\) to base 10.\n2. Multiply the base 10 equivalents.\n3. Convert the product back to base 7.\n4. Find the base 7 sum of the digits of the product.\n\n**Step 1: Convert \\(24_7\\) and \\(30_7\\) to base 10.**\n\nThe number \\(24_7\\) in base 10 is:\n\\[\n2 \\cdot 7^1 + 4 \\cdot 7^0 = 2 \\cdot 7 + 4 \\cdot 1 = 14 + 4 = 18\n\\]\n\nThe number \\(30_7\\) in base 10 is:\n\\[\n3 \\cdot 7^1 + 0 \\cdot 7^0 = 3 \\cdot 7 + 0 \\cdot 1 = 21 + 0 = 21\n\\]\n\n**Step 2: Multiply the base 10 equivalents.**\n\nThe product of \\(18\\) and \\(21\\) in base 10 is:\n\\[\n18 \\cdot 21 = 378\n\\]\n\n**Step 3: Convert the product \\(378_{10}\\) back to base 7.**\n\nTo convert \\(378_{10}\\) to base 7, we need to divide the number by 7 and keep track of the remainders.\n\n\\[\n378 \\div 7 = 54 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 0\n\\]\n\\[\n54 \\div 7 = 7 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 5\n\\]\n\\[\n7 \\div 7 = 1 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 0\n\\]\n\\[\n1 \\div 7 = 0 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 1\n\\]\n\nReading the remainders from bottom to top, we get \\(378_{10} = 1050_7\\).\n\n**Step 4: Find the base 7 sum of the digits of the product.**\n\nThe digits of \\(1050_7\\) are \\(1, 0, 5, 0\\). The sum of these digits is:\n\\[\n1 + 0 + 5 + 0 = 6\n\\]\n\nThus, the base 7 sum of the digits of the product is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{6}\n\\]",
